 "response": "Gikistu's budget is now **$3098K**. This comes from resolving every withdrawal, including withdrawals of withdrawals, and then applying the remaining Finance Office changes in order.\n\n**Messages ignored.** Only Finance Office budget messages count. PMO, Engineering, Sales, Legal and other notes were left out, as were Finance Office messages that don't change the budget (room moves, audits, invoice batches).\n\n**Resolving withdrawal chains.** A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect, so each chain was worked back from its latest entry. Some examples:\n- #0694 voids #0535, so #0435 stands. #0435 voids #0357, so #0206 stands. #0206 voids #0202, so #0145 stands. #0145 voids #0011, so #0005 stands. Result: update #0003 is withdrawn.\n- #0843 voids #0754, so #0019 stands. #0019 voids #0008. Result: update #0002 still applies.\n- #1556 voids #1554, so #0053 stands. Result: update #0050 is withdrawn.\n- #1500 voids #1310. Result: update #0852 still applies.\n- #1570 voids #1445. Result: update #0980 still applies.\n\nIn total, 119 budget updates end up withdrawn. Examples include #0003, #0012, #0014, #0030, #0525, #0600, #0861, #0885, #1029 and #1304.\n\n**Applying the remaining updates.** The budget starts at $2070K (#0001). Each remaining increase or decrease was then applied in record order, giving a final total of $3098K.\n\nANSWER: $3098K",
